{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"}],"title":"Service Reference"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for "},{"code":"RevenueCatPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — the RevenueCat-backed "},{"code":"PaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformer that the paywall plugin consumes."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"RevenueCatPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" adapts ","type":"text"},{"code":"RevenueCat.Purchases","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to the ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" protocol that ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall.PaywallPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" requires. It does one job: translate ","type":"text"},{"code":"CustomerInfo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" into ","type":"text"},{"code":"EntitlementSnapshot","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (defined by "},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") so the plugin can drive its state. Configuration of the RevenueCat SDK itself remains the caller’s responsibility."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a step-by-step integration walkthrough, see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/HowToImplementService"},{"type":"text","text":". For the entitlement-mapping rules, see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/EntitlementMapping"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Library-target","level":2,"text":"Library target","type":"heading"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Product: ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Import: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Package.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":[".product(name: \"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\", package: \"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\"),"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Types","text":"Types"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"``doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywallService``","anchor":"docSwiduxRevenueCatPaywalldocumentationSwiduxRevenueCatPaywallRevenueCatPaywallService"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public struct RevenueCatPaywallService: PaywallService {","    public init(","        entitlementID: String,","        permanentLicenseEntitlementID: String? = nil","    )","","    public func customerInfo() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot","    public func customerInfoStream() -> AsyncStream<EntitlementSnapshot>","    public func restorePurchases() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot","    @MainActor public func logIn(appUserID: String) async throws(RevenueCatPaywallIdentityError) -> RevenueCatPaywallIdentityResult","    @MainActor public func logOut() async throws(RevenueCatPaywallIdentityError) -> RevenueCatPaywallIdentityResult","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Value type. Holds two ","type":"text"},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" identifiers and forwards configured calls to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Purchases.shared"},{"type":"text","text":". It is safe to construct before "},{"code":"RevenueCatPaywall.configure","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" runs. For production, wrap it in SwiduxPaywall’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ResilientPaywallService"},{"text":" so a transient read failure at launch never gates a paid user as free.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Initializer","text":"Initializer","level":4,"type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public init(","    entitlementID: String,","    permanentLicenseEntitlementID: String? = nil",")"]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"entitlementID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — RevenueCat entitlement identifier that grants pro access. Surfaces as "},{"code":"EntitlementSnapshot.isPro","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when active."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"permanentLicenseEntitlementID"},{"type":"text","text":" — Optional secondary identifier for a lifetime \/ permanent entitlement. Surfaces as "},{"code":"EntitlementSnapshot.hasPermanentLicense","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when active. Pass ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" if the app has no separate lifetime SKU."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywall\/configure(apiKey:appUserID:userDefaults:logLevel:entitlementVerification:purchasesAreCompletedBy:storeKitVersion:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" before invoking the service. Construction before configuration is safe, including from a stored-property initializer. Previews and tests that do not configure RevenueCat should still use ","type":"text"},{"code":"MockRevenueCatPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when they need entitlement values.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Important"},{"anchor":"customerInfo-async-throws-%3E-EntitlementSnapshot","type":"heading","level":4,"text":"`customerInfo() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One-shot fetch. Calls "},{"code":"Purchases.shared.customerInfo()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and maps the result. A response older than five minutes by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"requestDate"},{"type":"text","text":" is labelled "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".cache"},{"type":"text","text":" (see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/EntitlementMapping#Live-and-cached-customer-info","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Throws ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywallError\/notConfigured","type":"reference"},{"text":" before configuration, ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywallError\/verificationFailed","type":"reference"},{"text":" for failed signature verification, or an SDK error. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"ResilientPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" can serve a valid same-account cache after a failed read; without a fallback the plugin dispatches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".refreshFailed(message)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"`customerInfoStream() -> AsyncStream<EntitlementSnapshot>`","anchor":"customerInfoStream-%3E-AsyncStream%3CEntitlementSnapshot%3E","type":"heading","level":4},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Long-lived stream. Wraps ","type":"text"},{"code":"Purchases.shared.customerInfoStream","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and yields a new ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntitlementSnapshot"},{"text":" for each valid change RevenueCat reports. A failed-verification element is skipped.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The stream finishes when the underlying RevenueCat stream finishes. The plugin’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".observeCustomerInfo"},{"text":" effect normally keeps it alive for the duration of the session; cancel by cancelling the consuming ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"text":", which terminates the stream and tears down the bridge.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Before configuration, the stream logs a fault and finishes immediately. Swidux 1.9 and later clears its observation guard when the stream ends, so configure RevenueCat and dispatch "},{"code":".observeCustomerInfo","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" again to retry."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The stream buffers only the newest snapshot: each yield is a complete entitlement state, so a slow consumer sees the latest value rather than replaying stale intermediate states.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A new stream first yields the customer info RevenueCat last delivered in this process, if any. RevenueCat may not have delivered one yet — on a relaunch with a fresh cache it skips the launch fetch — and then the stream stays silent until the next change, so dispatch ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".refreshCustomerInfo"},{"type":"text","text":" alongside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".observeCustomerInfo"},{"type":"text","text":" to seed the state."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":4,"anchor":"restorePurchases-async-throws-%3E-EntitlementSnapshot","text":"`restorePurchases() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot`","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps the result of RevenueCat’s user-initiated "},{"code":"restorePurchases()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" flow in every purchase-completion mode. Unlike "},{"code":"syncPurchases()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", this flow refreshes the App Store receipt and can recover a subscription missing from the device receipt. It may show an App Store sign-in prompt and applies the RevenueCat project’s restore behavior when purchases belong to another app user ID. It throws "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywallError\/notConfigured","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" before configuration, "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywallError\/verificationFailed","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for failed signature verification, or an SDK error."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin’s ","type":"text"},{"code":".restorePurchases","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" action wraps this call and dispatches ","type":"text"},{"code":".customerInfoUpdated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on success or ","type":"text"},{"code":".refreshFailed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on error.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":4,"text":"Identity operations","anchor":"Identity-operations"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"logIn(appUserID:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"logOut()"},{"type":"text","text":" switch the RevenueCat identity and map the returned customer info with the same entitlement identifiers and verification policy as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerInfo()"},{"type":"text","text":". Their "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywallIdentityResult","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" reports the identity observed after the call, whether it differs from the identity observed before the call, and the mapped snapshot. An already-anonymous logout skips the SDK logout operation and may return "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for its snapshot when no cached customer info passes the verification policy."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Failed signature verification is rejected. With "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"entitlementVerification: .disabled"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".notRequested"},{"type":"text","text":" responses are accepted without a signature check."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"All package login\/logout calls are serialized through completion, including the deprecated namespace methods. Direct RevenueCat identity calls bypass that serialization. A returned result records the completed operation; later queued operations may change the identity again.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both methods throw "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywallIdentityError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" instead of exposing RevenueCat errors. The error records the operation, a package-owned reason, and the identity observed before and after the failure. A provider operation can change identity before a later request or verification step fails, so callers must inspect "},{"code":"identityChanged","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" rather than treating every thrown error as an unchanged identity."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Identity results do not reset "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallState"},{"type":"text","text":", clear "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ResilientPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" caches, or reject delayed work from the previous identity. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/HeirloomLogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/issues\/46"},{"type":"text","text":" owns that integration contract. The customer-info stream may later repeat a successful operation’s result, but a failed offline transition is not guaranteed to yield a stream value."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Entitlement-mapping","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Entitlement mapping"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomerInfo"},{"type":"text","text":" the service receives:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Configuration"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isPro"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hasPermanentLicense"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"entitlementID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" active","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"(next column)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"entitlementID"},{"type":"text","text":" inactive or missing"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"(next column)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"permanentLicenseEntitlementID == nil"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"—"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"permanentLicenseEntitlementID"},{"type":"text","text":" active"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"—","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"permanentLicenseEntitlementID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" inactive or missing"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"—","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"}]}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both flags are checked independently against the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomerInfo"},{"type":"text","text":". A user with both active subscription and lifetime entitlements gets both flags set. See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/EntitlementMapping","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the reasoning behind the truth table."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/ServiceReference"},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/servicereference"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/HowToImplementService","doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/EntitlementMapping","doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/MockServiceReference","doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywallService","doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywallError","doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywallIdentity","doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywallIdentityResult","doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywallIdentityError"],"title":"Related Documentation"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/MockServiceReference","doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/UIComponentsReference"],"anchor":"Reference","title":"Reference"}],"references":{"doc://SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/documentation/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/UIComponentsReference":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/uicomponentsreference","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"UI Components Reference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the paywall, customer-center, and composed view modifiers in "},{"code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywallUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/UIComponentsReference"},"doc://SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/documentation/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/RevenueCatPaywallError/verificationFailed":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywallError\/verificationFailed","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"verificationFailed","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"RevenueCatPaywallError.verificationFailed","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/revenuecatpaywallerror\/verificationfailed","abstract":[{"text":"The response or a configured entitlement failed signature verification, so no snapshot was produced.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"https://github.com/HeirloomLogic/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/issues/46":{"title":"Issue #46","type":"link","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/HeirloomLogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/issues\/46","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/HeirloomLogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/issues\/46","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Issue #46"}]},"doc://SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/documentation/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/RevenueCatPaywallIdentityResult":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RevenueCatPaywallIdentityResult","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RevenueCatPaywallIdentityResult","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywallIdentityResult","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"RevenueCatPaywallIdentityResult","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/revenuecatpaywallidentityresult","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The completed state of a login or logout operation."}]},"doc://SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/documentation/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/EntitlementMapping":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How RevenueCat’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomerInfo.entitlements"},{"text":" translates to Swidux’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntitlementSnapshot"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/EntitlementMapping","title":"Entitlement Mapping","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/entitlementmapping","kind":"article","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/documentation/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/RevenueCatPaywallIdentity":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RevenueCatPaywallIdentity","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/revenuecatpaywallidentity","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"RevenueCatPaywallIdentity","abstract":[{"text":"A provider-independent description of the active purchase identity.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywallIdentity","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RevenueCatPaywallIdentity","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/documentation/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/RevenueCatPaywallService":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RevenueCatPaywallService"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RevenueCatPaywallService"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywallService","type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/revenuecatpaywallservice","kind":"symbol","title":"RevenueCatPaywallService","abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" conformer backed by RevenueCat’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Purchases.shared"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/documentation/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/RevenueCatPaywallError":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Errors "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywallService","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" raises itself, as opposed to errors it propagates from the RevenueCat SDK."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/revenuecatpaywallerror","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RevenueCatPaywallError","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywallError","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RevenueCatPaywallError"}],"title":"RevenueCatPaywallError"},"doc://SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/documentation/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/RevenueCatPaywallIdentityError":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A package-owned failure from a login or logout operation."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/revenuecatpaywallidentityerror","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RevenueCatPaywallIdentityError","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywallIdentityError","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RevenueCatPaywallIdentityError","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"RevenueCatPaywallIdentityError"},"doc://SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/documentation/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","type":"topic","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall","kind":"symbol","title":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"RevenueCat adapter for Swidux’s "},{"code":"PaywallPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Implements "},{"code":"PaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" against ","type":"text"},{"code":"Purchases.shared","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ships a controllable mock for previews and tests, and pairs with ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywallUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for drop-in ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"CustomerCenterView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" presentation.","type":"text"}]},"doc://SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/documentation/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/EntitlementMapping#Live-and-cached-customer-info":{"title":"Live and cached customer info","abstract":[],"kind":"section","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/EntitlementMapping#Live-and-cached-customer-info","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/entitlementmapping#Live-and-cached-customer-info"},"doc://SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/documentation/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/RevenueCatPaywall/configure(apiKey:appUserID:userDefaults:logLevel:entitlementVerification:purchasesAreCompletedBy:storeKitVersion:)":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywall\/configure(apiKey:appUserID:userDefaults:logLevel:entitlementVerification:purchasesAreCompletedBy:storeKitVersion:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"configure","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"apiKey","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","k